* The Towers of Hanoi by recursion. To move n discs from peg a to peg b:
* move n-1 from a to c, move one from a to b, move n-1 from c to b.
* JOSS has no arguments, so the pegs are exchanged before each inner
* move and exchanged back after it.
1.1 Done if n = 0.
1.2 Set n = n-1.
1.3 Do part 2.
1.4 Do part 1.
1.5 Do part 2.
1.6 Type a, b in form 1.
1.7 Do part 3.
1.8 Do part 1.
1.9 Do part 3.
1.95 Set n = n+1.

* Part 2 exchanges b and c. Part 3 exchanges a and c.
2.1 Set t = b.
2.2 Set b = c.
2.3 Set c = t.

3.1 Set t = a.
3.2 Set a = c.
3.3 Set c = t.

Form 1:
Move a disc from peg _ to peg _

Set a = 1.
Set b = 3.
Set c = 2.
Set n = 3.
Do part 1.
